<p>India has criticized a social media repost by President Donald Trump that amplified comments describing India as a &quot;hellhole&quot; while arguing against birthright citizenship and immigration in the United States. India&#x27;s Ministry of External Affairs called the remarks &quot;obviously uninformed, inappropriate and in poor taste,&quot; turning a message about US domestic immigration into a diplomatic irritant between two countries that are usually close partners. The episode comes just ahead of a planned visit to India next month by US Secretary of State Marco Rubio, as Washington tries to turn the page on recent strains in the relationship. It has also sparked broader public and political reaction in India, with opposition figures and former diplomats saying New Delhi should respond more forcefully, while some outside voices used the moment to highlight India&#x27;s culture and heritage instead.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0yZnrseSy5CkpOrGIfY1pkTSiS-Of-hrEeh5D8V-wDP6UNd_1tQA-NlMXp9vrK7DN88rB698X41ENdYeEWiyAKgJQBMtVpr9eulk1Bvu7Bv7A8tmCNUmK4MMFcbaaCoDp2JOnvq_DXyva4-W0dAAxC73NDNDSRz3OjzJo0yPjAP9G0cz-Q2zBxVlbspWnZuQOaq88aUjpmrz170F1W0dO6xUpC6sMOIkNBmp4qNGN1qVsXtx3baR3BgDdiSAo50UvVPrbmxk5ilNpUEizW-S' alt='Image accompanying coverage of India&#x27;s response to President Trump&#x27;s repost.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rubio trip: The dispute has surfaced shortly before Secretary of State Marco Rubio&#x27;s planned India visit next month, a trip described as an effort to turn the page on recent tensions between the normally friendly powers.</li><li>Political pressure: India&#x27;s foreign ministry responded after opposition members and former diplomats criticized the government for not answering Washington more forcefully.</li><li>Post source: Trump shared material from conservative pundit Michael Savage, whose comments targeted India and China during a debate over birthright citizenship and immigration policy.</li><li>Cultural pushback: Iran&#x27;s Consulate General in Mumbai answered with a video celebrating Maharashtra&#x27;s cultural and geographic heritage and said President Trump needed a &quot;cultural detox&quot;.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>India&#x27;s Ministry of External Affairs: Spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal publicly condemned the remarks as uninformed and inappropriate, signaling official displeasure without announcing retaliatory steps. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/hellhole-on-the-planet-trump-reposts-critique-targeting-india-china-over-birthright-citizenship/article70896776.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Indian opposition and former diplomats: Critics at home pressed the government to answer Washington more firmly, arguing that its response did not go far enough. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/hellhole-on-the-planet-trump-reposts-critique-targeting-india-china-over-birthright-citizenship/article70896776.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iran&#x27;s Consulate General in Mumbai: The consulate used the controversy to spotlight India&#x27;s cultural richness, posting a video about Maharashtra and inviting President Trump to see the country for himself. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-iran-live-news-irans-cultural-detox-jibe-at-trump-over-hell-hole-remark-kabhi-india-aa-ke-dekho-11401854#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/india-criticises-poor-taste-trump-post-against-immigrants'>India criticises ‘poor taste’ Trump post against immigrants</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/hellhole-on-the-planet-trump-reposts-critique-targeting-india-china-over-birthright-citizenship/article70896776.ece'>Trump shares right-wing anchor’s rant against Indians, MEA terms it ‘inappropriate’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351218/china-or-india-or-some-other-hellhol